		<item>
			<title>Madonna's Masterpiece did NOT qualify for Oscar contention!</title>
			<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/361-madonnas-masterpiece-did-not-qualify-for-oscar-contention.html</link>
			<guid>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/361-madonnas-masterpiece-did-not-qualify-for-oscar-contention.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p><span id="articleText">
<p>BREAKING NEWS - That's incredible! Once again the <strong>Academy</strong> proved to hate <strong>Madonna</strong>! The <strong>Academy</strong> announced the 39 qualifying songs  in this year's race, but, despite being nominated for a <strong>Golden Globe</strong>, <strong>Madonna</strong>'s <strong>Masterpiece</strong> is missing on the list.</p>
<p> </p>
<p><strong>Masterpiece</strong> did not qualify for <strong>Oscar</strong> contention because of  its placement a minute-and-a-half deep in the final credits. Apparently AMPAS rules  require an end-credits song to be "the first music cue" in those  credits to qualify.</p>
</span></p></div><div class="K2FeedTags"><ul><li>W.E.</li><ul></div>]]></description>
			<category>Movies</category>
			<pubDate>Mon, 19 Dec 2011 23:02:48 +0000</pubDate>
